# Generated files from regression tests
*/backend
*/backend.zig
*/backend.err
*/compile_backend.err
*/compile_kz.err
*/compile_intermediate.err
*/compile_zig.err
*/intermediate
*/intermediate.zig
*/output
*/output.zig
*/output_emitted
*/output_emitted.zig
*/actual.txt
*/a.out

# Ignore all files without extensions (likely binaries)
*

# Keep directories (at any depth)
!*/

# Keep source and expected files (at any depth)
!**/*.kz
!**/*.k
!**/*.kjs
!**/*.kc
!**/*.kgpu
!**/expected.txt
!**/expected_output.txt
!**/expected_error.txt
!**/expected_patterns.txt
!**/expected_comptime.txt
!**/expected.json
!**/EXPECT
!**/EXPECT_TIMEOUT
!**/EXPECT_TRAP
!**/COMPILE_ONLY
!**/SKIP
!**/MUST_*
!**/SHOULD_*
!**/PARSER_TEST
!**/LANGUAGES
!**/ARGS
!**/STDIN
!**/input.txt
!**/*.data

# Keep documentation and marker files (at any depth)
!**/README.md
!**/*.md
!**/.MARKER
!**/TODO
!**/RULING
!**/NEEDS_RULING
!**/PRIORITY
!**/BENCHMARK
!**/BROKEN
!**/BUG_*
!**/THRESHOLD

# Keep scripts (at any depth)
!**/post.sh
!**/*.sh

# Keep baseline files for performance tests (at any depth)
!**/baseline.zig
!**/fixture.zig
!**/baseline.go
!**/*.go
!**/baseline.rs
!**/COMPILER_FLAGS
!**/*.c
!**/koru.json

# Keep benchmark comparison files
!**/*.py
!**/*.lua

# Keep vendored fixtures and their pins (std/vendor tests). A vendored tree is
# checked-in third-party source — it IS the fixture, and its contents are what
# the pin is taken over, so every byte has to survive a fresh clone. Scoped to
# `vendored/` so the blanket `*.zig` artifact ignore above still holds elsewhere.
!**/vendored/**
!**/vendor.lock
